          "kind": "file", "perms": "-rw-r--r--", "owner": "tech", "group": "union", "size": "0", "mtime": "091-01-01 00:00",
          "_notes": "The console's ls color scheme, as real editable content rather than hardcoded GDScript -- Dan's 'bashrc for this machine' idea, 2026-09-04. No in-game text editor exists yet to let a player edit this live; that's the natural next step this file sets up for. Console.gd reads it at load time (ContentLoader.parse_conf-style key=value) with hardcoded fallbacks if a key or the file itself is missing.",
          "content": "COLOR_DIR=#5c9cff\nCOLOR_SYMLINK=#00d7d7\nCOLOR_DEVICE=#d7d700\nCOLOR_EXEC=#00d700\n"
        },
        "aliases": {
          "kind": "file", "perms": "-rw-r--r--", "owner": "tech", "group": "union", "size": "0", "mtime": "118-09-02 14:02",
          "_notes": "Real shell aliases, same 'editable content, not hardcoded' pattern as consolerc -- Console.gd checks a command's first word against this before normal dispatch. ll/la are the universal muscle-memory ones; the rest are Scrapshell-specific shortcuts for the diagnostic loop this machine actually does day to day.",
          "content": "ll=ls -la\nla=ls -la\nmydev=ls -la dev\ncheck=probe rfc2305 --node self\n"
        }
      }
    },
